#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Linearizability checker for atomic range transactions.

Each request is a completed concurrent history of whole transactions (a
transaction is one atomic operation).  A witness is a serial order of the
transactions that respects real time (A.end <= B.start => A before B), in which
every observed return value matches and the resulting map equals the final map.

The checker searches serial orders with depth first search over
(prefix-of-witness, state) nodes, memoising failed nodes.  Each transaction is
compiled into a small Python function that applies its operations to a state
tuple (returning None when an observation would not match), which keeps the
inner loop fast.  Sound necessary-condition prunes (based on which values the
remaining transactions can still write / still need to read) cut off hopeless
subtrees early.

Reads newline delimited JSON requests from stdin, writes one JSON object per
input line to stdout: {"order": [...]} or {"order": null}.
"""

